From: mx65w-poe-build <noreply@example.com>
Date: Thu, 6 Oct 2026 19:05:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ARM: dts: broadcom: add BCM59111 PSE node to Meraki MX65

Declares the Broadcom BCM59111 PoE PSE controller on i2c0 so the
bcm59111 hwmon driver can bind via device tree. max_power_mw matches
the 60 W PSE budget reported by the hardware.

Signed-off-by: mx65w-poe-build <noreply@example.com>
---
--- a/arch/arm/boot/dts/broadcom/bcm958625-meraki-alamo.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm/boot/dts/broadcom/bcm958625-meraki-alamo.dtsi
@@ -280,3 +280,14 @@
 		};
 	};
 };
+
+&i2c0 {
+	bcm59111@21 {
+		compatible = "brcm,bcm59111";
+		pagesize = <32>;
+		reg = <0x21>;
+		ports = <2>;
+		port_base = <0>;
+		max_power_mw = <60000>;
+	};
+};
